    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The verb bracket with separable verbs",
     "texto": [
      "Separable-prefix verbs (**aufstehen, anfangen, einkaufen, fernsehen**) form a syntactic bracket (*Satzklammer*) in the main clause:",
      "1. The base verb is conjugated and takes the **second position** (or the first in yes/no questions).",
      "2. The separable prefix goes in the **last place in the sentence**, closing the idea:",
      "**aufstehen** (to get up) → Ich **stehe** um sieben Uhr **auf**.",
      "**einkaufen** (to do the shopping) → Carlos **kauft** am Samstag **ein**.",
      "**anfangen** (to start) → Der Sprachkurs **fängt** am Montag **an**.",
      "**fernsehen** (to watch TV) → Abends **sehen** wir **fern**.",
      "If the sentence has several complements (time, day, company), they all go in the middle of the bracket, between the conjugated verb and the final prefix."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
